"A2780","Time(h)":96,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"0.303 ± 0.068","IC50_Dark_value":0.303,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/ic401535s","Year":2013,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-034856","value":"2.31 ± 0.06","numeric":2.31}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-034857","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"I","Cell_line":"HCT-116","Time(h)":96,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"1.478 ± 0.430","IC50_Dark_value":1.478,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/ic401535s","Year":2013,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-034857","value":"7.6 ± 1.70","numeric":7.6}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-034858","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"I","Cell_line":"MCF-7","Time(h)":96,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"2.467 ± 0.051","IC50_Dark_value":2.467,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/ic401535s","Year":2013,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-034858","value":"4.8 ± 0.80","numeric":4.8}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-035463","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"1a","Cell_line":"MDA-MB-231","Time(h)":96,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"9.5 ± 0.7","IC50_Dark_value":9.5,"Method":"Crystal violet","DOI":"10.1039/c4dt03105a","Year":2014,"Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"I","value":1.13,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1093/mtomcs/mfac056","year":2022,"record_id":"MLDB-004343","detection":"ICP-OES","method_description":"The lipophilicity of compounds was determined by measuring the octanol : water partition coefficient, log P, using a shake flask method, according to OECD.36 Deionized water and n-octanol were presaturated for 24 h under stirring. The stock solutions of the compounds were prepared by dissolving proper amounts in 25 ml of presaturated deionized water to a final concentration of 0.5 mmol · L-1.36 The samples were prepared by adding 7.5 ml of the stock solution plus 7.5 ml of presaturated 1-octanol and shaken for two hours. Then, they were centrifuged for phase separation. The aqueous phases (7.0 ml) were treated with an equivalent volume of aqua regia 50% (V/V) to remove all organic matter. The solutions were heated and concentrated to dryness. After drying the entire solution, the sample was calcined at 773,15 K for 20 min. A stock solution sample was measured to calculate the total amount of gold. For analysis, the material was solubilized in aqua regia 1.0% (V/V) and was analyzed in duplicate by ICP-OES, following the methodology adapted from Klose and colleagues.44 The partition coefficient P was calculated by the concentration in aqueous and organic phases and expressed as log P. The samples were prepared in duplicates and analyzed in two independent experiments."}],"ccdc":["CTPPAU"]}